{{Term/Store|Tingle's Hood||Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
Tingle's Hood is a piece of [[Armor]] that [[Link]] can wear on his head. It is exclusive to {{TMT}} [[Downloadable Content]] Pack. Alongside [[Tingle's Shirt]] and [[Tingle's Tights]], it is part of the [[Tingle's Outfit]] [[Armor Set]].<ref name="CaC 188"/> When all pieces are worn together, Link's speed at night will be increased.

Tingle's Hood was stolen from [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]] with other pieces of Tingle's Outfit by [[Misko]].<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> During the "[[EX Treasure: Fairy Clothes]]" [[Side Quest]], Link is tasked with finding ''[[Misko's EX Journal]]'' to learn where it has been hidden.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> In the ''Journal'', the Hood is said to be within the "ruins where trade flourished.<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal"/> At the [[Outpost Ruins]], Link can find a [[Hidden Chest]] embedded in the ground, which contains Tingle's Hood.<ref name="BotW Adventure Log 2"/>

After obtaining Tingle's Hood, [[Granté]] will begin to sell it from 50 [[Rupee]]s in [[Tarrey Town]].{{Note|Prior to the [[The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild#Updates|Version 1.3.3 Update]], Granté would not sell any Armor that is exclusive to the {{BotWEP}}. This meant that Tingle's Hood could not be replaced if sold, which was noted in its [[Inventory]] description.<ref name="BotW Inventory 2"/>}} Tingle's Hood is unable to be [[Hateno Dye|Dyed]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] or upgraded at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].

